<title>USA: Cash America self-tender offer expires.</title>
<headline>Cash America self-tender offer expires.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash America International Inc said on Wednesday that the preliminary results of its &quot;Dutch Action&quot; self-tender offer, which expired Tuesday indicate that 6,362,041 shares of common stock were tendered and not withdrawn at prices of $8.50 per share or lower.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to purchase 4,500,000 shares tendered at such price, or about 70.7 percent of the shares tendered at the $8.50 price.</p>
<p>Following the purchase of shares tendered in the offer, the company will have about 24,259,454 shares of common stock outstanding.</p>
